Feature: Heikin-Ashi Reversal at RSI Extremes
  Primary timeframe: 1h
  Parameter streak default 3
  Parameter oversold default 35
  Parameter overbought default 65
  Parameter stop_loss_pct default 1.5
  Parameter take_profit_pct default 3

  # Heikin-Ashi reversal primitives time the entries; an RSI extreme confirms
  # exhaustion. Strong-HA-candle primitives close the trade on momentum against
  # the position. Tight percentage stops/targets suit the intraday timeframe.

  Scenario: Enter long on a bullish HA reversal from oversold
    Given no open position
    When ha_bullish_reversal(streak)
    And rsi_oversold(oversold)
    Then long_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 + take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit long on a strong bearish HA candle
    Given a long position is open
    When ha_strong_bearish()
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Enter short on a bearish HA reversal from overbought
    Given no open position
    When ha_bearish_reversal(streak)
    And rsi_overbought(overbought)
    Then short_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 + stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 - take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit short on a strong bullish HA candle
    Given a short position is open
    When ha_strong_bullish()
    Then short_exit
